  "retained": [
    "Q4/Q5 batched scale/min extraction uses bit masks instead of divergent lower/upper cases. Scalar decoding retains its existing extraction. Floating-point products, sums and reduction order are unchanged.",
    "Use uint32 device indices when weight byte offsets and input/output element offsets all fit; retain size_t for larger matrices. The guard uses division, with compile-time overflow-boundary checks.",
    "Q4 retains two staging tiles at large FFN widths 5–8 and grouped width-4 work for the small width-8 projection. Q5 uses two tiles at FFN widths 5–7; width 8 uses eight waves/four output rows, removing the first prototype’s register spill.",
    "Q6 FFN widths 5–8 reuse activations across three output rows/two tiles. Q6 vocabulary widths 7/8 use bounded uint32 indices with the existing three-row layout.",
    "Extend the existing GEMM ablation tool; no new executable, environment switch or CLI control."
  ],
